01:25:43.000 --> 01:25:46.040
UUIDs out there in the world.

01:25:46.040 --> 01:25:50.640
And to summarize, a UUID is basically a randomly generated ID, right?

01:25:50.640 --> 01:25:55.840
So instead of every record having an ID that just increments by one number, you'll be generating

01:25:55.840 --> 01:25:59.920
a very large random number as your ID for every record.

01:25:59.920 --> 01:26:04.640
And again, the nice thing about that is you don't have to do a read before you do an insert

01:26:04.640 --> 01:26:10.080
because you can just kind of generate a huge number randomly and be fairly confident that

01:26:10.080 --> 01:26:15.360
and when I say fairly, I mean extremely, like it's essentially mathematically, it's nearly

01:26:15.360 --> 01:26:20.720
impossible to have duplicate UUIDs because there's just so many possible combinations.

