Now we're going to work with the or operator.

02:15:28.540 --> 02:15:34.200
So it works very similarly to the and operator, but instead of both conditions on either side

02:15:34.200 --> 02:15:42.280
of the or keyword needing to evaluate to true, only one does, right?

02:15:42.280 --> 02:15:44.120
And to be clear, it's okay if both do.

02:15:44.120 --> 02:15:46.800
So at least one side needs to evaluate to true.

02:15:46.800 --> 02:15:49.720
At least one condition needs to evaluate to true.

02:15:49.720 --> 02:15:55.160
And it's also worth pointing out that the order of operations can be manipulated with

02:15:55.160 --> 02:15:56.160
parentheses.

02:15:56.160 --> 02:16:01.520
So in this case, we're saying we're going to evaluate this and that first.

02:16:01.520 --> 02:16:06.040
And then the result of that is going to be ordered with the other, right?

02:16:06.040 --> 02:16:12.520
So we can use parentheses, just like in math, to adjust the order of operations.

