02:22:00.600 --> 02:22:04.360
So still working with the like clause, we're going, we're going to take a look at another

02:22:04.360 --> 02:22:05.880
operator basically.

02:22:05.880 --> 02:22:13.600
So the, the percent operator or the percent sign, like I said, matches zero or more characters.

02:22:13.600 --> 02:22:19.680
Whereas the underscore operator matches exactly one character, right?

