Next question, which would not match example two?

02:24:24.640 --> 02:24:32.560
So we've got two underscores here, bling that matches sling that matches thing that

02:24:32.560 --> 02:24:36.080
matches singing does not match too many characters, right?

02:24:36.080 --> 02:24:41.800
This, this only has room for five characters.

02:24:41.800 --> 02:24:45.440
New keyword, we've got the limit keyword.

02:24:45.440 --> 02:24:52.120
Now this one, this might be one of the keywords that I use the absolute most in SQL apart

02:24:52.120 --> 02:24:57.520
from like the obvious things like select and where limit is super, super common, both when

02:24:57.520 --> 02:25:01.560
you're writing application code, as well as when you're just kind of making one off queries

02:25:01.560 --> 02:25:06.000
to a database, because it's very often the case that when you're working on a production

02:25:06.000 --> 02:25:11.240
scale database, a table doesn't just have six or seven or 10 rows like what we've been

02:25:11.240 --> 02:25:14.000
dealing with in our little sandbox environment, right?

02:25:14.000 --> 02:25:20.520
We could have a thousand rows, we could have a million rows, we could have 100 million

02:25:20.520 --> 02:25:21.840
rows in the database.

02:25:21.840 --> 02:25:27.800
And if you try to just select all of those rows, something's going to crash, right?

02:25:27.800 --> 02:25:31.120
That's a lot of data to pull out of a database all at once.

02:25:31.120 --> 02:25:35.520
So that's where the limit keyword becomes really, really useful.

02:25:35.520 --> 02:25:36.840
Here's what it looks like.

02:25:36.840 --> 02:25:44.200
So after any select statement, we can end it with this limit, this limit section here

02:25:44.200 --> 02:25:49.840
we're saying, just give me 50, do not give me more than 50 rows, right?

02:25:49.840 --> 02:25:52.280
Give me up to 50.

02:25:52.280 --> 02:25:57.920
So if my query was only going to return three rows anyways, the limit keyword effectively

02:25:57.920 --> 02:26:00.040
would do nothing here.

02:26:00.040 --> 02:26:08.160
But if like, you know, 7000 products match this query, we're going to stop the database

02:26:08.160 --> 02:26:11.400
and say, just give me the first 50, give me the first 50.

02:26:11.400 --> 02:26:12.400
Okay.

