You don't need to see every single record to get a feel for like what all the columns

02:27:34.160 --> 02:27:37.240
are and what kind of data is actually in those columns.

02:27:37.240 --> 02:27:40.720
You'd typically just kind of like connect to the database, run a simple query like this,

02:27:40.720 --> 02:27:45.080
maybe limit it to 10 or 20 or 30 rows that you can fairly easily scan through.

02:27:45.080 --> 02:27:48.400
That's something I find myself doing a lot as a backend developer.

02:27:48.400 --> 02:27:49.400
Cool.

02:27:49.400 --> 02:27:51.560
I'm going to go ahead and submit that.

02:27:51.560 --> 02:27:58.400
So this question here says, limit five will always return five records and the answers

02:27:58.400 --> 02:27:59.400
are true and false.

02:27:59.400 --> 02:28:03.120
And the reason this is false, I'll just go ahead and click that now.

02:28:03.120 --> 02:28:09.080
The reason this is false is because if the query were only going to return zero or one

02:28:09.080 --> 02:28:16.280
or two records anyways, then limit five isn't going to add records, right?

02:28:16.280 --> 02:28:18.800
It's just saying, don't give me more than five.

