02:53:05.920 --> 02:53:11.840
It takes the value to be rounded and the precision that we want to round the value to, but it

02:53:11.840 --> 02:53:17.560
is really common to use the round function when you're dealing with the results of an

02:53:17.560 --> 02:53:18.560
aggregation.

02:53:18.560 --> 02:53:25.280
By default, if we do not pass in a value for the precision parameter, by default, SQL will

02:53:25.280 --> 02:53:29.280
just round it to the nearest whole number, at least SQL lite will.

