03:00:49.760 --> 03:00:55.920
It's important to remember that SQL is technically a full programming language.

03:00:55.920 --> 03:01:00.520
Now, like I said, at the beginning of the course, we don't typically use SQL to build

03:01:00.520 --> 03:01:02.680
out full applications from scratch, right?

03:01:02.680 --> 03:01:07.080
It is a domain specific language in the sense that it's intended to be a query language,

03:01:07.080 --> 03:01:12.080
a language used to interact with databases, but it is a programming language, right?

03:01:12.080 --> 03:01:13.080
It has functions.

03:01:13.080 --> 03:01:15.960
It has ways to do these sorts of things.

