So employees is in this case table A. Inner join departments, in this case departments

03:57:56.880 --> 03:58:02.200
is table B. And now we have this new keyword, the on keyword,

03:58:02.200 --> 03:58:05.800
which is used in tandem with a join.

03:58:05.800 --> 03:58:09.280
So this describes how we're going to join.

03:58:09.280 --> 03:58:11.320
It describes that key relationship.

03:58:11.320 --> 03:58:20.520
So inner join departments on employees dot department ID equals departments dot ID.

03:58:20.520 --> 03:58:28.000
So in this case, we're saying we want all of the rows where on the employees table,

03:58:28.000 --> 03:58:34.400
the department ID matches a row in the departments table with that same ID.

